abstract: 'Yi guan lue shu san shu [Brief account of a medical institution: Three
  writings] is a Chinese hospital publication catalogued as 1874, with [Foochow] supplied
  as its place of publication and 柯為樑 (Dauphin William Osgood) credited with revision.
  Its charitable and missionary statements, hospital narratives, illustrations, donor
  lists and financial tables support research on medical charity, fundraising and
  institutional publishing. Based on 24 images of Bodleian Sinica 1634, the dataset
  provides TXT, JSON and TEI XML for 42 designated physical faces, with uncertainties
  and source mappings. The provisional AI transcription includes selected source-image
  corrections; full human double collation and expert review have not been performed.'
